From its use as creative expression to documenting our everyday reality, photography has become an essential and widely-accessible medium since its invention. Did you know, however, that the technology was developed in France? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha takes a look at the French legacy of photography.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73198654-e4fc-11f1-ab3a-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-01-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73198654-e4fc-11f1-ab3a-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-01-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8fe9f34a-e4fc-11f1-952f-318618d819ba</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:28:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France investigates actor Depardieu, writer Houellebecq over alleged gang rape</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-france-investigates-gerard-depardieu-writer-houellebecq-over-alleged-gang-rape</link><description>
French police are investigating allegations actor and convicted sex offender Gérard Depardieu raped and assaulted a woman with the complicity of bestselling author Michel Houellebecq during a 2018 film shoot, two sources following the case said Friday. The plaintiff has accused the film's director Guillaume Nicloux of being complicit in the abuse.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c09677fe-e4f5-11f1-add1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7ZY6NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c09677fe-e4f5-11f1-add1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7ZY6NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d92e1a20-e4f4-11f1-a526-c7c3772058c8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:27:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c09677fe-e4f5-11f1-add1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7ZY6NQ.jpg">© Joël Saget, Dimitar Dilkoff, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title><![CDATA['Blade Runner 2099' & 'Rivals': The big TV shows to watch this month]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261120-blade-runner-2099-rivals-the-big-tv-shows-to-watch-this-month</link><description>
"Blade Runner" returns with a futuristic twist, while British bonkbuster "Rivals" is back with part two of season two. TV critic Dheepthika Laurent joins Eve Jackson to review the month’s big releases, including Netflix’s acclaimed Arctic comedy "North of North" and the lavish K-drama "Remarried Empress".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2680dcea-e4e6-11f1-8ca4-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-BLADE-RUNNER-2099-frame-658.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2680dcea-e4e6-11f1-8ca4-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-BLADE-RUNNER-2099-frame-658.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef07b85a-e4e6-11f1-81d6-0f52e66a5e0e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:17:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Eve JACKSON</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gen Z protests spread across Europe: Mass rallies over cost of living in Spain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-gen-z-protests-spread-across-europe-mass-rallies-over-cost-of-living-in-spain</link><description>
Protesters across Europe are set took to the streets on Friday in a show of cross-border solidarity, joining coordinated demonstrations against the rising cost of living, militarisation and other causes, in a bid to increase pressure on their governments. Protesters across Europe are set to take to the streets on Friday in a show of cross-border solidarity, joining coordinated demonstrations against the rising cost of living, militarisation and other causes, in a bid to increase pressure on their governments. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3bcbfdf2-e4f8-11f1-a072-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-160358-160755-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3bcbfdf2-e4f8-11f1-a072-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-160358-160755-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4148bc66-e4f8-11f1-ba7a-01a00b14daa6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:41:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French ex-PM Villepin announces presidential run</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-french-ex-pm-villepin-announces-presidential-run</link><description>
France's former prime minister and foreign minister Dominique de Villepin, famed abroad for his excoriating 2003 denunciation of US plans for invading Iraq, said on Friday he was running for president. Villepin enters an already crowded field of candidates seeking to succeed President Emmanuel Macron, with polls pointing towards a possible run-off between frontrunner Marine Le Pen of the far-right National Rally (RN) and hard-left France Unbowed (LFI) veteran Jean-Luc Melenchon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b230c90-e4f8-11f1-9b3d-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-160931-161049-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b230c90-e4f8-11f1-9b3d-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-160931-161049-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60c5874a-e4f8-11f1-8000-5f83eba11166</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:40:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>Shenzhen trilateral: Xi Jinping's 'masterclass in diplomatic theatre'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261120-shenzhen-trilateral-xi-jinping-s-masterclass-in-diplomatic-theatre</link><description>
Xi Jinping positioned himself as a great statesman when he met with the US president and Russia's Vladimir Putin for trilateral talks in Shenzhen this week. But while the Chinese president sparkled on the world stage, does he have anything to show for it? Seong-Hyon Lee, an associate at Harvard University Asia Center, tells us how the trilateral has come up short on deliverables.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2bb9420a-e4f1-11f1-aeb6-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/TRUMP-JINPING-POUTINE-000-D7XR8CA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2bb9420a-e4f1-11f1-aeb6-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/TRUMP-JINPING-POUTINE-000-D7XR8CA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">157a2bc8-e4ef-11f1-a363-9125c0ae01ff</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:37:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Delano D’SOUZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Spain’s political crossroads, Europe’s wider stakes: Spaniards to vote in key election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election</link><description>
The stakes are high – not only for people in Spain, but also for Europe. On November 29, the country holds a parliamentary election that could see the end of the Socialist-led government and potentially a coalition between the right and the far right, in one of the EU’s biggest and most influential member states. It could also signal the end of Pedro Sanchez’s third term in office. Among other things, the prime minister may pay the political price for two shocking train crashes and the migrant crisis in Spain’s North African exclave of Ceuta. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb70dc0a-e434-11f1-8bdf-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-SPAIN-DEBATE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb70dc0a-e434-11f1-8bdf-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-SPAIN-DEBATE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64fa5a54-e1a9-11f1-b476-43a8f9a2efe8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:17:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>Jamaica's beaches are increasingly off limits to locals</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels</link><description>
Jamaica usually conjures up images of white sandy beaches, Rastafari culture and Bob Marley – but another reality exists. On this small Caribbean island, less than 1 percent of the coastline is freely accessible to local people. The rest has gradually been privatised, mostly for large hotel developments and private homes.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1952df8c-e41e-11f1-b8ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1952df8c-e41e-11f1-b8ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e9372ab0-e431-11f1-9387-ff4fa45f9015</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:55:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Laurence CUVILLIER</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Cincinnati Zoo's famed Fiona the hippo dies days after eating a visitor’s hat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-cincinnati-zoo-s-famed-fiona-the-hippo-dies-days-after-eating-a-visitor-s-hat</link><description>
Fiona, the hippo whose premature birth and fight for survival at the Cincinnati Zoo turned her into a global sensation nearly a decade ago, died Thursday from complications after swallowing a knit hat that was accidentally flung into her enclosure. She was 9 years old. “It is with extreme sadness that we share with you the devastating news that Fiona did not make it after multiple attempts from our amazing vets and keeper team to help her through what ended up being a medical emergency,” the zoo said in a statement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ea273a-e4ef-11f1-a4bb-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-135316-135437-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ea273a-e4ef-11f1-a4bb-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-135316-135437-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f611b106-e4ef-11f1-a824-b3bef9076718</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:48:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Burnham, Von der Leyen hail 'turning point' in EU-UK relations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-replay-burnham-von-der-leyen-hail-turning-point-in-eu-uk-relations</link><description>
British Prime Minister Andy Burnham hailed a "landmark" deal with the European Union on Friday, as the two sides sealed pacts on food exports, emissions-trading schemes and youth mobility at a summit in Brussels. EU chief Ursula von der Leyen welcomed a "turning point" in ties with Britain following Brexit. Watch our replay.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28039ada-e4f0-11f1-9a52-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-140752-144607-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28039ada-e4f0-11f1-9a52-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-140752-144607-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2d05e272-e4f0-11f1-9bcb-bf5d2765226b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:45:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>COP31 wrapping up in Turkey: Climate deal elusive as fossil fuels go unmentioned</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-cop31-wrapping-up-in-turkey-climate-deal-elusive-as-fossil-fuels-go-unmentioned</link><description>
The UN's COP31 climate talks were set to spill into overtime Friday as countries remained deadlocked over a draft deal that makes no mention of fossil fuels, with a host of other disputes also snarling negotiations. The talks come with a series of stark reminders of the urgency of climate action, from heatwaves in Europe and devastating floods in Nepal, while a record-breaking El Nino supercharges temperatures. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/846de880-e4ef-11f1-8515-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-151225-151557-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/846de880-e4ef-11f1-8515-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-151225-151557-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89987e06-e4ef-11f1-89be-770637ba5815</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:38:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Burnham hails 'landmark' EU-UK deal as 'good day' for Britain, Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-burnham-hails-landmark-eu-uk-deal-as-good-day-for-britain-europe</link><description>
Britain and the European Union agreed deals on trade, carbon emissions and youth movement on Friday, and pledged to rebuild ties with an “ambitious and dynamic” post-Brexit relationship. In a joint statement after a summit in Brussels, the UK and EU confirmed agreements that will scrap checks on the trade in plant and animal products, link their emissions trading schemes and let 100,000 young adults from each side live and work in the other's countries for up to three years. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb0ce690-e4ee-11f1-9c3c-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-150057-150653-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb0ce690-e4ee-11f1-9c3c-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-150057-150653-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0085038c-e4ef-11f1-8614-5119e2ea797f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:37:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia pummels Ukraine with massive strikes, missile hits Poland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-russia-pummels-ukraine-with-massive-strikes-missile-hits-poland</link><description>
Moscow pounded Ukraine with massive strikes Friday, with Kyiv saying at least six people were killed in the capital, and neighbouring Poland reporting two Russian missiles likely landed in the south-east corner of the NATO country, accusing Moscow of a "provocation." Hours earlier, Russia's Vladimir Putin vowed a "painful" response to Kyiv's strikes on Moscow's Crimea bridge after holding a summit with China's Xi Jinping and US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv, Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eee66c42-e4ee-11f1-9776-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-150718-151143-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eee66c42-e4ee-11f1-9776-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-150718-151143-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f411d5d0-e4ee-11f1-a175-37b5afb88e61</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:36:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Scoop</category><title>'GTA VI': When the biggest-ever entertainment release becomes the biggest headline</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261120-gta-vi-when-the-biggest-ever-entertainment-release-becomes-the-biggest-headline</link><description>
This week FRANCE 24's media show "Scoop" looks at how the press covered the release of "Grand Theft Auto VI". Pre-orders and first-day sales totalled more than $2.3 billion. What does the game and the franchise's success mean for the future of entertainment? Our guest is Margaret Wallace, a video game developer and an associate professor of the practice of media innovation at Boston University.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b187bf8-d9ed-11f1-9fe5-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/Jason-and-Lucia-15.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b187bf8-d9ed-11f1-9fe5-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/Jason-and-Lucia-15.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6895f62-e4e2-11f1-8d6a-8139fcdfd2e9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:35:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>William HILDERBRANDT</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France probes suspected leak of confidential information to Le Pen's party</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-france-probes-suspected-leak-confidential-information-le-pen-far-right-party</link><description>
French authorities are investigating whether a former senior official at the Interior Ministry leaked confidential information about judicial investigations into far-right leader Marine Le Pen's National Rally, adding to the party's legal woes ahead of a presidential election next year in which Le Pen is the current frontrunner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed281fb0-e4ec-11f1-b121-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9QL2XA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed281fb0-e4ec-11f1-b121-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9QL2XA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a364bd6c-e4eb-11f1-9e9e-e983666fb240</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:35:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed281fb0-e4ec-11f1-b121-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/000-9QL2XA.jpg">© Pascal Guyot, AFP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>A decade after Brexit, do Britons regret leaving the EU?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-a-decade-after-brexit-do-britons-regret-leaving-the-eu</link><description>
Britain and the European Union went through a bitter divorce, then slowly began trying to rebuild their relationship. UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham met the EU's top officials in Brussels on Friday for a summit he has described as a step towards undoing a decade of damage caused by the 2016 vote to leave the bloc. But how do the British public feel about closer ties with the EU – and, potentially, rejoining it?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb35512e-e4ed-11f1-aa3f-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-140135-140337-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb35512e-e4ed-11f1-aa3f-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-140135-140337-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d07dd5fc-e4ed-11f1-968b-b372a4baed96</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:34:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>Does staggered consent actually protect young people?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people</link><description>
Following recent scandals involving two iconic British comedians, the UK government is considering the introduction of staggered age consent. Annette Young talks to Katherine Allen from the Institute of Social Justice and Crime in the UK about whether such laws work. Also the social costs of femicide; how do loved ones cope with such a loss, and what support is available to families in the wake of such a tragedy? Plus we meet the women who are challenging the traditions of Mexican mariachi music, a world that remains largely male dominated. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75df6f36-e4e6-11f1-8b81-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75df6f36-e4e6-11f1-8b81-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3cd92630-e4ca-11f1-a1e0-39177940782c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:14:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>El Salvador: Nayib Bukele, self-proclaimed “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term</link><description>
🇸🇻 El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele, who calls himself the “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term after changing the Constitution to scrap presidential term limits. His war on gangs has made him hugely popular, but also sparked serious human rights concerns.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86fc3e64-e4d9-11f1-a0c6-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/Salvador-00-01-50-03-Still001.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/86fc3e64-e4d9-11f1-a0c6-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/Salvador-00-01-50-03-Still001.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0535d34-e4d9-11f1-9010-ed28dec6c8cc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:07:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 France seeks UN Security Council meeting after Russian strikes hit European embassies in Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">8288fdbc-e4da-11f1-85c7-790c017cbaa5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:04:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Malaysia's unwanted refugees: The plight of the Rohingya</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261120-malaysia-s-unwanted-refugees-the-plight-of-the-rohingya</link><description>
On November 19, the International Court of Justice delivered a historic ruling: finding Myanmar guilty of committing genocide against the Rohingya in 2017. Malaysia has long been a supporter of the persecuted Muslim minority. But its role as a safe haven is coming to an end, amid a rise in hate speech and calls for the expulsion of Rohingya via social media. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4133a2c-e441-11f1-beda-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-MALAYSIA-ROHIGNYA-RACISM-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4133a2c-e441-11f1-beda-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-MALAYSIA-ROHIGNYA-RACISM-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a5ec6f0-e443-11f1-91a8-93c014f0cee0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:28:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Théo Collet</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Italy strike draws workers, students into nationwide protests over wages and living costs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-italy-strike-draws-workers-students-into-nationwide-protests-over-wages-and-living-costs</link><description>
A nationwide strike was expected to disrupt schools, hospitals and local transport across Italy on Friday as workers and students began marching in dozens of cities to demand higher wages, lower living costs and greater social protections. The labor action coincided with an International Day of Student Mobilisation, with organisers planning demonstrations in more than 45 Italian cities. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome, Italy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6abc8560-e4d4-11f1-87e1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-120355-120805-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6abc8560-e4d4-11f1-87e1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-120355-120805-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6fc110bc-e4d4-11f1-958d-c5ab6533dbce</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:25:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South Africa: High Court examines asylum seekers' detention at Lindela centre</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-south-africa-high-court-examines-asylum-seekers-detention-at-lindela-centre</link><description>
South Africa's High Court judges visited the Lindela Repatriation Centre in Krugersdorp this week, ahead of delivering a ruling on 33 urgent applications concerning the detention of asylum seekers. The court is examining conflicting interpretations of a Constitutional Court ruling that prohibits the deportation of asylum seekers whose claims are still being processed. The case comes amid a wider and increasingly tense debate over immigration in South Africa, which has at times spilled over into deadly xenophobic violence. FRANCE 24's Eunice Masson reports from Cape Town, South Africa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97aba57c-e4d1-11f1-be4a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-214548-215033-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97aba57c-e4d1-11f1-be4a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-214548-215033-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c7e5a72-e4d1-11f1-a5a8-398ac8fe108c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:23:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Our culture and identity': Deaf Nigerians embrace indigenous sign languages</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-our-culture-and-identity-deaf-nigerians-embrace-indigenous-sign-languages</link><description>
With a quick flick of the wrist, Umaru Zayyanu conveys the phrase "I am a Nigerian". But the 37-year-old is not signing, rather in the west African nation's official sign language. Instead, he's using Hausa sign language. Such indigenous sign languages abound in Africa's most populous country, where deaf people were communicating with each other long before the advent of formal sign language taught in deaf schools, in 1960.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d854d850-e4d1-11f1-89aa-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-215248-215434-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d854d850-e4d1-11f1-89aa-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-215248-215434-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddd4617e-e4d1-11f1-ae40-4f8dd2a0942f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:21:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
